![high](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/high-priority.svg)

In the `finally` block of `New-ControllerOneTimeRunnerLabel`, if an exception occurs during execution (e.g., in the `try` block), the cleanup statements may throw a `NullReferenceException` if `$rng` or `$bytes` is null (for example, if initialization failed or was partially completed). Any exception thrown in a `finally` block will discard and mask the original exception from the `try` block, making debugging extremely difficult. Additionally, we should explicitly validate that `$Config` and `$Config.github` are not null before accessing their properties under strict mode.

```
function New-ControllerOneTimeRunnerLabel {
    [CmdletBinding()]
    param([Parameter(Mandatory = $true)]$Config)
    if ($null -eq $Config -or $null -eq $Config.github) {
        throw 'Invalid configuration: github configuration section is missing.'
    }
    $prefix = [string]$Config.github.isolated_runner_label_prefix
    $randomByteCount = [int]$Config.github.isolated_runner_label_random_bytes
    if ($prefix -cne 'cie-jit-' -or $randomByteCount -ne 32) {
        throw 'One-time runner label policy must remain cie-jit- plus 256 random bits.'
    }
    $bytes = New-Object byte[] $randomByteCount
    $rng = [Security.Cryptography.RandomNumberGenerator]::Create()
    try {
        $rng.GetBytes($bytes)
        $label = $prefix + ([BitConverter]::ToString($bytes)).Replace('-', '').ToLowerInvariant()
    } finally {
        if ($null -ne $rng) { $rng.Dispose() }
        if ($null -ne $bytes) { [Array]::Clear($bytes, 0, $bytes.Length) }
    }
    if (-not (Test-ControllerOneTimeRunnerLabel -RunnerLabel $label -Config $Config)) {
        throw 'Generated one-time runner label failed the fixed format contract.'
    }
    return $label
}
```

