Under `Set-StrictMode -Version Latest`, accessing properties on a null object or missing properties on `$Config` will throw a terminating exception. To ensure the validation function fails closed gracefully and returns `$false` instead of throwing a cryptic strict-mode exception, wrap the property checks in a `try-catch` block and verify that `$Config` and `$Config.github` are not null.

```
function Test-ControllerOneTimeRunnerLabel {
    [CmdletBinding()]
    param(
        [Parameter(Mandatory = $true)][string]$RunnerLabel,
        [Parameter(Mandatory = $true)]$Config
    )
    try {
        if ($null -eq $Config -or $null -eq $Config.github) { return $false }
        if ([string]$Config.github.isolated_runner_label_prefix -cne 'cie-jit-') { return $false }
        if ([int]$Config.github.isolated_runner_label_random_bytes -ne 32) { return $false }
        return $RunnerLabel -cmatch '^cie-jit-[0-9a-f]{64}$'
    } catch {
        return $false
    }
}
